codex
The first proof attempt exposed a real limitation of the supplied semantics: end-relative indexing over an opaque symbolic `IntSeq` leaves the partial `intSeqAt` term undefined, so the prover cannot even decide the first Boolean operand. I’m reshaping the implementation to recurse on the left-stripped suffix; that gives the prover constructor-visible indices (0, 1, 2) while preserving the same rightmost-vowel algorithm.
